# Rakeez site · Apache (cPanel). Deploying is still copying files.
#
# The paths are ROOT-RELATIVE and must stay that way: Apache serves the error
# document at the URL that failed, so /a/b/c.html gets 404.html rendered under
# /a/b/, and a relative path would 404 inside the 404.
ErrorDocument 403 /403.html
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
ErrorDocument 500 /500.html

# 403 is otherwise the most likely error on a static site: a bare directory with
# no index. Turning listings off is what produces it — better a branded 403 than
# a file index of the docroot.
Options -Indexes
